# The Uses and Misuses of Central Registries in Child Protective Services

**Authors:** Gibelman, Margaret, Grant, Stuart

## Abstract
Reports results of a national survey on the use of computerized central registry systems as in child protective services, the perceived advantages and disadvantages of such systems and the extent to which protections have been established against potential abuse of individual civil rights. A need for further study of central registries is indicated. (CM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ183955

